\\sigma_{\\text{RM}} \\simeq \\left(\\frac{\\Delta R}{l_{\\text{s}}}\\right)^{1/2}\\delta\\text{RM}(l _{\\text{s}})  = \\frac{e^{3}}{2\\pi m_{e}^{2}c^{4}}(l_{\\text{s}}\\Delta R)^{1/2} \\delta(n_{e}B_{\\parallel})_{l_{\\text{s}}} = 0.81\\,\\,\\text{rad}\\,\\,\\text{m}^{-2}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{l_{\\text{s} }\\Delta R}}{1\\,\\,\\text{pc}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\delta(n_{e}B_{\\parallel})_{l_{ \\text{s}}}}{1\\,\\,\\text{cm}^{-3}\\mu\\text{G}}\\right), and the depolarization wavelength is

